00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:52.720
Don't know why it existed, and I wanted  to know more about it, but this is why, like,

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:57.620
These indie horror games that you find on Game Jolt, they're like a window into what could be

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:01.120
they're a little snippet of potential, and you see something good and you're like

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:07.640
OHH, this is cool! And then you remember; it's made by a small team and it's made in such a short amount of time, and you're just like-

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:13.500
OH, I want MORE! And this is made for an asylum jam, and it's like, there could be more out of this

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:20.280
And I want to see MORE... That's what I get out of these indie horror games- I wanna see more!

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:23.360
You see the talent, and you see what could be...

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:27.220
with these interesting very basic ideas, and when you see potential

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:28.280
It's like it's there, so either way!

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:31.820
